MID_SE_Urs_Sim_C: <EDH>
MID_SE_Urs_Sim_C_001: Hey, boss lady. This the embezzler you wanted?
MID_SE_Urs_Sim_C_002: It is, yes. He looks properly terrified...
MID_SE_Urs_Sim_C_003: I gave him the standard roughing up. You shouldn't\nhave any trouble getting answers out of him now.
MID_SE_Urs_Sim_C_004: P-please! Forgive me! I'll tell you whatever you\nwant—just don't hurt me any more!
MID_SE_Urs_Sim_C_005: You may be a war dog, Simon, but I do appreciate\nyour sense for efficiency. This shouldn't take long.
MID_SE_Urs_Sim_C_006: Now, to confirm, these fraudulent numbers are\nyour handiwork, no?
MID_SE_Urs_Sim_C_007: Yes... It was me. I admit it.
MID_SE_Urs_Sim_C_008: So, you'd take a share of cargo, claiming to be pulling\ndefective product, and then you'd sell it for profit...
MID_SE_Urs_Sim_C_009: Perhaps only a small amount each time, but it adds\nup, doesn't it? And makes you harder to catch...
MID_SE_Urs_Sim_C_010: Let's call it a loan... Though, given how long ago you\nstarted borrowing, the interest will be considerable.
MID_SE_Urs_Sim_C_011: H-hang on! How am I supposed to pay it all back\nwith interest?! There's no way!
MID_SE_Urs_Sim_C_012: These are the results of your actions. And should you\nfail to pay, we will seize and liquidate your assets.
MID_SE_Urs_Sim_C_013: How am I supposed to live like that? You might as\nwell just kill me!
MID_SE_Urs_Sim_C_014: We wouldn't be able to collect what we're owed\nfrom a dead man, would we?
MID_SE_Urs_Sim_C_015: Now, I have more questions. To start, who else\nwas involved?
MID_SE_Urs_Sim_C_016: I've given the order to apply pain as necessary, but\nit's hard to say how much we'll get out of him.
MID_SE_Urs_Sim_C_017: You scare me sometimes... But whatever it\ntakes, huh?
MID_SE_Urs_Sim_C_018: Parasites like him were a real nuisance in the time\nTalimun spent away.
MID_SE_Urs_Sim_C_019: Given their lingering presence, we must be thorough\nin rooting them out.
MID_SE_Urs_Sim_C_020: Cleaning up after our sleepyhead boss, eh?\nYou've got your work cut out for you.
MID_SE_Urs_Sim_C_021: I'm merely performing my duties as the person who\noversees the company's operations.
MID_SE_Urs_Sim_C_022: I'm sure Talimun could have managed the issue were\nhe here. There's still much I can learn from him.
MID_SE_Urs_Sim_C_023: You know, I used to think you were just\nTalimun's secretary...
MID_SE_Urs_Sim_C_024: But having seen you at work, I'd say you could run\nany merchant house you chose.
MID_SE_Urs_Sim_C_025: You're a capable woman, and you should know that.\nHell, I might fall for you after seeing you in action.
MID_SE_Urs_Sim_C_026: Heh. Is that so? And how much stock should I place\nin such words, I wonder.
MID_SE_Urs_Sim_B: <EDH>
MID_SE_Urs_Sim_B_001: Talimun! Where the hell are you?! You stole all\nmy customers! My business is ruined!
MID_SE_Urs_Sim_B_002: Hey! We got another one!
MID_SE_Urs_Sim_B_003: Talimun tends to crush his competition. Some, like\nthis man, feel they've been personally wronged.
MID_SE_Urs_Sim_B_004: But the fact is simply that we provide a service he is\nunable to match. Complaining will get him nowhere.
MID_SE_Urs_Sim_B_005: What do you hope to get out of this? Some kind of\nrevenge? Get out of here before I show you the door.
MID_SE_Urs_Sim_B_006: Damn it... This isn't over!
MID_SE_Urs_Sim_B_007: I never get bored working for this company. The boss\nhas a way of starting trouble wherever he goes.
MID_SE_Urs_Sim_B_008: I don't know how he manages to get into some\nof the situations he finds himself in...
MID_SE_Urs_Sim_B_009: But with you...I get the sense you go looking\nfor trouble.
MID_SE_Urs_Sim_B_010: Heh, you got me. That's why I like it here.\nI don't have to look very far.
MID_SE_Urs_Sim_B_011: Ever the dog chasing the kill.
MID_SE_Urs_Sim_B_012: Ouch. That's a bit harsh. Is that really what you\nthink of me?
MID_SE_Urs_Sim_B_013: In truth? Yes. I have no fondness for hired killers.
MID_SE_Urs_Sim_B_014: My family was murdered by a group of mercenaries\nwhen I was young. Before I came to Dagda.
MID_SE_Urs_Sim_B_015: And yet here we are, having a lovely conversation.\nLife's funny, isn't it?
MID_SE_Urs_Sim_B_016: Talimun trusts you, so I do as well. Nothing more.
MID_SE_Urs_Sim_B_017: Hehehe. Say what you will, but I think you like him\ntelling you what to do.
MID_SE_Urs_Sim_B_018: I would happily do anything Talimun asked of me.
MID_SE_Urs_Sim_B_019: It's my job to quash any petty squabbles. Such trivial\nmatters are beneath Talimun.
MID_SE_Urs_Sim_B_020: He must be free to pursue his ambitions, whatever\nthose may be.
MID_SE_Urs_Sim_B_021: As long as he can do that, I'm willing to make what\nsacrifices I must. In fact, I'm happy to.
MID_SE_Urs_Sim_B_022: Huh. You've been calling me his war dog all this\ntime, but it sounds to me like you're his lapdog.
MID_SE_Urs_Sim_B_023: Whaddaya say we two dogs just keep wagging our\ntails and enjoying our boss's treats, then, hm?
MID_SE_Urs_Sim_B_024: Hmhm. Now there's something we can agree on.
MID_SE_Urs_Sim_A: <EDH>
MID_SE_Urs_Sim_A_001: I've been reflecting, and...we've both been with the\ncompany for some time now, haven't we?
MID_SE_Urs_Sim_A_002: Sure, but I haven't been around nearly as long\nas you have.
MID_SE_Urs_Sim_A_003: We've attached ourselves to the same guy though.\nWe're stuck together, you and I.
MID_SE_Urs_Sim_A_004: That may be so...
MID_SE_Urs_Sim_A_005: So, you tell Talimun how you feel yet?
MID_SE_Urs_Sim_A_006: I— That is none of your business.
MID_SE_Urs_Sim_A_007: Are you scared or something? Of what? He's a good\nguy—and you're an incredible woman.
MID_SE_Urs_Sim_A_008: If he ever dumps you, though, don't forget about me.
MID_SE_Urs_Sim_A_009: Need a rebound? I'll be right there, waiting with\nopen arms. So, you have nothing to lose, right?
MID_SE_Urs_Sim_A_010: That's...very generous, but I'll have to decline.
MID_SE_Urs_Sim_A_011: I've looked into your past. You've had many war-zone\nromances, and you always leave when the war ends.
MID_SE_Urs_Sim_A_012: You're a soldier of fortune who puts what he wants\nover all else. But what I want is to not be abandoned.
MID_SE_Urs_Sim_A_013: Hehe. Of course. But on the other hand, as long as\nthere's a fight to be had, I'm sure to stick around.
MID_SE_Urs_Sim_A_014: I have to imagine you could find a way to keep\nthis old war dog fed, couldn't you?
MID_SE_Urs_Sim_A_015: I do find it easier to put others' needs first once\nmine have been satisfied...
MID_SE_Urs_Sim_A_016: You aren't serious...are you?
MID_SE_Urs_Sim_A_017: I dunno. What if I was?
MID_SE_Urs_Sim_A_018: Doesn't matter in the end, does it? Talimun would\nnever let a woman like you slip through his fingers.
MID_SE_Urs_Sim_A_019: Simon... You...
MID_SE_Urs_Sim_A_020: Look, forget about me. Just go tell Talimun you love\nhim already.
MID_SE_Urs_Sim_A_021: It's true! Which means the two of you are stuck\nwith me.
MID_SE_Urs_Sim_A_022: Hmm.
MID_SE_Urs_Sim_A_023: Anyway, sorry. I didn't mean to take up so much of\nyour time with my yapping. I'll be going. Good luck.
MID_SE_Urs_Sim_A_024: Thank you, Simon.